"donor_log2fc":-0.0058966,"donor_lfcse":0.071819,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.17791e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"C1S","gene_symbol_current":"C1S","gene_id":"ENSG00000182326","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":2.41837e-08,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.20147,"nucleus_score":-5.73682,"pct_ad":0.0914238,"pct_control":0.104277,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.553131,"donor_log2fc":-0.213621,"donor_lfcse":0.0978341,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0303187}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000182326","module":"black","kme":0.206349,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":1.0,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000182326","entrez_id":["716"],"uniprot":["P09871"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a serine protease, which is a major constituent of the human complement subcomponent C1. C1s associates with two other complement components C1r and C1q in order to yield the first component of the serum complement system. Defects in this gene are the cause of selective C1s deficiency. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P09871","text":"Component of the complement C1 complex, a multiprotein complex that initiates the classical pathway of the complement system, a cascade of proteins that leads to phagocytosis and breakdown of pathogens and signaling that strengthens the adaptive immune system (PubMed:11445589, PubMed:16169853, PubMed:417728, PubMed:467643, PubMed:6271784, PubMed:6282646, PubMed:6319179, PubMed:70787, PubMed:9422791). C1S is activated following association of the C1 complex with immunoglobulins (IgG or IgM) complexed with antigens to form antigen-antibody complexes on the surface of pathogens (PubMed:34155115). C1S is cleaved and activated by C1R to generate C1s subcomponent heavy and light chains (PubMed:11445589, PubMed:6271784). C1s subcomponent light chain then cleaves and activates C2 and C4, the next components of the classical complement pathway (PubMed:16169853, PubMed:467643, PubMed:6282646, PubMed:6319179, PubMed:6906228, PubMed:70787, PubMed:9422791). [Complement C1s subcomponent light chain]: Serine protease component of the complement C1 complex, which catalyzes cleavage and activation of C2 and C4, the next components of the classical complement pathway (PubMed:16169853, PubMed:22949645, PubMed:417728, PubMed:467643, PubMed:6282646, PubMed:6319179, PubMed:70787, PubMed:9422791). Also able to cleave C1 inhibitor (SERPING1) in vitro; additional evidence is however required to confirm this result in vivo (PubMed:16169853). Also cleaves IGFBP5 and thereby inhibits the trophic effects of IGF1 (PubMed:18930415)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}